	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Tanaris is the great desert of southern {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. Its dunes run from the cliffs of {link:thousand-needles}Thousand Needles{/link} to the southern sea, and from the green rim of {link:un-goro-crater}Un'Goro Crater{/link} to a coast of warm beaches and hidden coves. Rain almost never falls. Every well is worth killing for, and every pool of water draws something thirsty. In the north stands {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link}, a walled goblin town that has made a trade out of water. Around it the sands keep older things: the broken temples of the trolls, the sealed stone gates of a place called {link:valley-of-the-watchers}Uldum{/link}, and a great cave in the eastern cliffs where the dragons of time are said to dwell.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle says when the land became a desert, or what it was before. The trolls are its oldest remembered masters. In the days of their empire, a tribe of desert trolls raised the city of {red:zul-farrak}Zul'Farrak{/red} among the northern dunes, and scattered shrines and towns across the sands to the south and east. Most of these now lie in ruins. Older still are the works of the titans. In the south-west, in the {link:valley-of-the-watchers}Valley of the Watchers{/link}, giant statues stand before sealed gates that no living hand has opened, and scholars who study the {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link} discs believe that those gates and the titans' records are bound together.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Tanaris belongs to whoever can hold water. The goblins of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link} rule {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link}, and their water company pumps the town's wells. Outside the walls, the {link:wastewander-nomads}Wastewander nomads{/link} have seized nearly every other well in the desert. Now something worse has come. Swarms of insects have risen from the sand in the west and south, and they are draining the pools dry. The scholars of Gadgetzan call them the {link:qiraji}silithid{/link}, and they fear that a mind stands behind them. {link:ogres}Ogres{/link} of the Dunemaul have built a camp in the southern waste. The {link:sandfury-trolls}Sandfury trolls{/link} watch from Zul'Farrak. On the coast, pirates of {link:southsea-pirates}the Southsea{/link} hold a walled cove only a short walk south of the Cartel's port.

The Cartel is not idle. Its ships still sail from {link:steamwheedle-port}Steamwheedle Port{/link} to {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link}, and a newer route carries them to {link:powderfuse-port}Powderfuse Port{/link} in the {link:riverglades}Riverglades{/link}, on the far side of the sea.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The goblins of {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link}.{/b} Engineers, alchemists, smiths and merchants who sell to anyone, and whose bruisers make sure that no one fights inside the walls.
• {b}The {link:wastewander-nomads}Wastewander nomads{/link}.{/b} Bandits and thieves of the eastern sands, who hold the wells and sell the water back to the thirsty.
• {b}The {link:sandfury-trolls}Sandfury trolls{/link}.{/b} The desert tribe of Zul'Farrak and of the ruins around it, known for cruelty and dark magic.
• {b}The silithid.{/b} Insects of the Centipaar hives, who have dug their lairs in the {link:the-noxious-lair}Noxious Lair{/link} and the {link:the-gaping-chasm}Gaping Chasm{/link}.
• {b}The Dunemaul ogres.{/b} A band of nomads newly come to the southern desert.
• {b}The {link:southsea-pirates}Southsea pirates{/link}.{/b} Freebooters who prey on Cartel ships from {link:lost-rigger-cove}Lost Rigger Cove{/link}.
• {b}Beasts of the sand.{/b} Basilisks with hides like glass, scorpids, hyenas, great firebirds, and the walking thistleshrubs of the south-west.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Troll Empire.{/b} The desert trolls built Zul'Farrak and worshipped a great hydra they called Gahz'rilla. Carved ornaments of that god still lie buried in the sands of their old towns.
• {b}The Coming of the Cartel.{/b} In later ages, the goblins of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link} came to the desert and built {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link} and {link:steamwheedle-port}Steamwheedle Port{/link}. No chronicle records the year.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The wells are lost, the insects are rising, and the town that sells water has begun to hire every sword it can find.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Sands",
			text = [=[• Travellers who die in the desert near {link:gadgetzan}Gadgetzan{/link} are buried in a small graveyard outside its walls. It is said that a spirit named Gaeriyan waits in the hills to the north, and that he speaks only to those who have crossed over.
• A lost turtle named Tooga wanders the desert in search of his wife Torta, who waits for him south of {link:steamwheedle-port}Steamwheedle Port{/link}.
• The goblins of Gadgetzan say that the rum of Steamwheedle Port is as thick as gravel and burns like lava. They mean it as praise.]=],
		},
	},
})

